                  <provenance type="#s"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_4">Canterbury, Kent.
                        Benedictine cathedral priory of Holy Trinity or Christ Church</orgName><p>Cotton Otho D. viii fols. 8–173, and Cambridge, Trinity
                        College, O. 2. 51, flyleaves, are fragments of one volume.</p><p>The hand is
                        recognisably that of Christ Church.</p><p>The flyleaves bear the 13th-cent.
                        title 'Passionale sancti Ignacii . primum', which corresponds to the wording
                        of an entry in the Eastry catalogue from the cathedral.</p><p>End part of
                        contents list (= items 18–26 in Otho D.viii) on front flyleaf of Trinity,
                        title on end flyleaf of Trinity.</p><p>See Ancient Libraries, p. 52, no.
                        360.</p><note type="MLGB3_medievalCatalogueNotes">Cat.
                     360</note></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Wm. Bowier (see CCCC 298, art. 19, extract
                     'ex quodam vetusto libro quondam ecclesie Cantuar. iam in manibus mri Bower.
                     Liber vocatur passionale S. Ignatii'.</provenance>
               </history>
